\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces PI-VIFT. Orange: what it adds to the base network. Besides the visual and inertial latents, each edge token carries a preintegration token and a state token. The head outputs 18 residual corrections; the physics step adds them to a kinematic prediction (rotation $\Delta \mathbf  R_k$ from the gyroscope, translation from the carried velocity, gravity and the preintegrated acceleration), updates velocity, gravity and biases edge by edge, and carries the state to the next window. $\Delta \mathbf  R_k,\Delta \mathbf  v_k,\Delta \mathbf  p_k$ come from preintegrating the IMU window with the current biases.}}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:pivift}{{4}{5}{PI-VIFT. Orange: what it adds to the base network. Besides the visual and inertial latents, each edge token carries a preintegration token and a state token. The head outputs 18 residual corrections; the physics step adds them to a kinematic prediction (rotation $\Delta \mathbf R_k$ from the gyroscope, translation from the carried velocity, gravity and the preintegrated acceleration), updates velocity, gravity and biases edge by edge, and carries the state to the next window. $\Delta \mathbf R_k,\Delta \mathbf v_k,\Delta \mathbf p_k$ come from preintegrating the IMU window with the current biases}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5}{\ignorespaces Gate decisions. (a) Direction: fused where network and geometry agree within their combined uncertainty, geometry where they clearly disagree, network otherwise; without geometry, v4 holds the last gated direction once the network is distrusted. (b) Length: the accelerometer where its window is observable, the network elsewhere. Rotation always comes from the gyroscope. v3 uses a fixed $\sigma _{\mathrm  {net}}=0.83^\circ $; v4 replaces it by the online $\hat  \sigma $.}}{5}{figure.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:gate}{{5}{5}{Gate decisions. (a) Direction: fused where network and geometry agree within their combined uncertainty, geometry where they clearly disagree, network otherwise; without geometry, v4 holds the last gated direction once the network is distrusted. (b) Length: the accelerometer where its window is observable, the network elsewhere. Rotation always comes from the gyroscope. v3 uses a fixed $\sigma _{\mathrm {net}}=0.83^\circ $; v4 replaces it by the online $\hat \sigma $}{figure.5}{}}
